 ## Overview
-Voxel-based Ray Tracing is a global illumination (GI) and specular reflection fallback method that uses Digital Differential Analyzer (3D-DDA) traversal through a uniform block-occupancy voxel grid to sample indirect lighting and reflections [S1, unofficial]. It serves as a drop-in replacement for Screen-Space Ray Tracing (SSRT) for GI and a fallback for Screen-Space Reflections (SSR) when coverage is incomplete, combining sky occlusion with Light Propagation Volumes (LPV) colour bleeding [S1, unofficial]. Unlike sibling methods that may rely on screen-space data alone, this method leverages a pre-computed 3D voxel grid populated in the shadow pass to provide scene-wide illumination data [S1, unofficial].
+Voxel-based Ray Tracing is a global illumination (GI) and specular reflection fallback method that uses Digital Differential Analyzer (3D-DDA) traversal through a uniform block-occupancy voxel grid to sample indirect lighting and reflections [S1, unofficial]. It serves as a drop-in replacement for Screen-Space Ray Tracing (SSRT) for GI and a fallback for Screen-Space Reflections (SSR) when coverage is incomplete, combining sky occlusion with Light Propagation Volumes (LPV) colour bleeding [S1, unofficial]. Unlike sibling methods that rely solely on screen-space data, this method leverages a pre-computed 3D voxel grid populated in the shadow pass to provide scene-wide illumination data [S1, unofficial].
 
